# Plain-text charts

Hovers and inlay tooltips draw with Unicode blocks, so every editor shows them.

## Countdown progress

[review_session] := countdown(40m, 16m)

<!-- Hover review_session: the tooltip shows ████░░░░░░ 40% with the elapsed time. -->
Time left: [review_session.remaining].

- [ ] Review the quarterly numbers @timer(review_session) @estimate(40m)

## Checklist progress :launch

<!-- Hover the heading name or its inlay: ████████░░ 80% with 4/5 complete. -->

- [x] Draft the announcement
- [x] Collect screenshots
- [ ] Record the demo video :demo
  - [x] Write the script
  - [ ] Capture the recording
- [x] Update the changelog

<!-- Hover the parent task: its tooltip shows a subtask bar, █████░░░░░ 50%. -->

Launch is [completed(launch)] of [total(launch)] steps done.

## Sparklines

[sales] := table
| month | units | revenue |
| ----- | ----- | ------- |
| Jan   | 12    | $1,200  |
| Feb   | 18    | $1,710  |
| Mar   | 9     | $990    |
| Apr   | 24    | $2,400  |
| May   | 21    | $1,995  |

<!-- Hover the units or revenue column header for a sparkline and its range. -->
<!-- Hover the sum below: row contributions start with a sparkline. -->
[average_price] := sum(sales, revenue) / sum(sales, units)
[total_units] := sum(sales, units)

We sold [total_units] units at an average of [average_price] each.
